    "created_at": "2019-03-03T10:02:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-03-03T10:02:16Z",
    "body": "Yes, there should be only one `fullscreenchange` event for entering and exiting fullscreen each time. The even is dispatched to the target element (and bubble all the way up to the window) by default. There is one exception that, when exiting fullscreen, if the element has been disconnected from the document, the event would be fired to the document. But either case, there is only one event.\r\n\r\nI guess we can close this issue now?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
